fn generate_github_alternative_url(url: &str) -> Option<(ureq::Agent, String)> {
  if !url.starts_with("https://github.com/") {
    return None;
  }

  generate_github_mirror_url_from_template(url)
    .or_else(|| generate_github_mirror_url_from_base(url))
    .map(|_alt_url| {
      (
        ureq::Agent::config_builder()
          .user_agent(BUNDLER_USER_AGENT)
          .build()
          .into(),
        url.to_owned(),
      )
    })
}

findings.body:
In `generate_github_alternative_url`, the closure now takes `_alt_url` and returns `url.to_owned()`. The mirror URL built from `TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR_TEMPLATE` or `TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR` is thrown away, so `create_agent_and_url` always receives the original `github.com` URL. Users who set these variables to reach WiX or NSIS through a mirror will see downloads go straight to GitHub and fail on networks where it is blocked. The tests only cover `generate_github_mirror_url_from_template`, so nothing catches this.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="52-58"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The user-agent change is the only intended effect of this block. The URL should still come from the mirror helper.

Suggested fix:

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="52-58"}
.map(|alt_url| {
  (
    ureq::Agent::config_builder()
      .user_agent(BUNDLER_USER_AGENT)
      .build()
      .into(),
    alt_url,
  )
})

The `tauri` field in `metadata-v2.json` is bumped to `2.9.3`, but `crates/tauri/Cargo.toml` is still at `2.9.2`. This file is embedded via `include_str!` in `crates/tauri-cli/src/init.rs`, `info/mod.rs`, and `plugin/init.rs`. `cargo tauri init` writes that value into new projects as the `tauri` dependency version, so newly generated projects would depend on a version that does not exist on crates.io or in this tree. The other fields (`tauri-build`, `tauri-plugin`) are unchanged, which suggests the `tauri` bump was made by mistake or as a side effect of the CLI version bump.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="1-9"}

Either revert the `tauri` field to `2.9.2`, or bump `crates/tauri` as part of the same release and confirm the intent.
